! Cl ATOM | ISOLATED BASIS SANITY CHECK
!
! ============================================================
! Why this file exists
! ============================================================
! A forum reply questioned the ~274 Hartree energy difference we found
! between our wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP/PCM(water) molecular energy (-491.67) and
! the energy reported in the original (lower-level) IRC source file
! (-765.88) at the same geometry. Re-checking this:
! - The arithmetic is correct (-765.8776395 - (-491.6712565) = -274.2).
! - The CML file's molecule was confirmed identical: 13 atoms, Cl/C/C/O/H/H/
!   O/O/H/H/H/H/H, same composition, same electron count (60).
! - A back-of-envelope sum of literature non-relativistic atomic HF energies
!   for this composition (Cl approx -459.5, C approx -37.7 x2, O approx
!   -74.8 x3, H approx -0.5 x7) gives approximately -763 Hartree for the
!   separated atoms -- very close to the CML's -765.88, and NOT close to
!   our own -491.67.
! - This is NOT explained by an accidental ECP: GAMESS explicitly reports
!   NUMBER OF ELECTRONS = 60 in every one of our runs (an ECP replacing
!   Cl's Ne core would show a reduced count, e.g. 50), and our own $clbas
!   block has an appropriately tight core exponent (69507.99) for Cl's 1s
!   shell, consistent with genuine all-electron treatment.
! - Also confirmed NOT a "forgot to add nuclear repulsion" bookkeeping
!   error: THE NUCLEAR REPULSION ENERGY IS 292.6267568387 is a SEPARATELY
!   printed quantity, and GAMESS's "FINAL ... ENERGY IS" line already
!   includes it by standard convention (self-consistent: a very negative
!   electronic energy plus positive nuclear repulsion gives the reported
!   total, as expected).
!
! This points at something specific to how our own basis/setup describes
! chlorine, since Cl's atomic energy alone (~-459.5) is close in magnitude
! to a large fraction of the unexplained gap. Rather than keep reasoning
! from recalled reference numbers, this file tests it directly and
! empirically: an isolated Cl atom, gas phase, no PCM, no molecule, no
! optimizer -- using our EXACT $clbas block (copied verbatim from
! caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPe.inp, not retyped, to rule out a new
! transcription error). If our basis/setup is fine, the reported energy
! should land close to the literature non-relativistic reference
! (approximately -459.5 Hartree for HF; DFT should be in a similar overall
! ballpark, not off by hundreds of Hartree). If it comes out dramatically
! different, that pinpoints the problem directly and unambiguously.
!
! Cl ground state is 2P (one unpaired electron in the 3p shell), so this
! uses SCFTYP=UHF (doublet, MULT=2). Note: ROHF was tried first but requires
! explicit NSETO/NPAIR orbital-coupling input for chlorine's genuinely
! degenerate 3p5 open shell (5 electrons across 3 degenerate p-orbitals) --
! plain MULT=2 alone isn't enough information for ROHF's coupling scheme,
! and GAMESS aborted with "DIMENSIONS EXCEEDED". UHF sidesteps this (fills
! alpha/beta orbitals independently, no coupling setup needed) and is fine
! for this purpose -- a rough energy-magnitude sanity check, not a
! symmetry-pure atomic term energy.

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=UHF RUNTYP=ENERGY DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         MULT=2 ICHARG=0 NOSYM=1 MAXIT=200
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS BASNAM(1)=clbas $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=20 MEMDDI=20 $END

 $DATA
Isolated chlorine atom -- def2-TZVPP basis sanity check
C1
Cl   17.0   0.0   0.0   0.0
 $END


